Here's a simple JavaScript function that accepts text and posts it to a Slack channel using the Slack API:

```javascript
const axios = require('axios');

function postMessageToSlack(text, channel) {
  const url = `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage?token=${process.env.SLACK_TOKEN}&channel=${channel}`;
  const data = {
    'text': text,
    'as_user': true
  };

  return axios.post(url, data);
}

// Example usage
postMessageToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general').then(response => {
  console.log('Message posted successfully:', response.data);
}).catch(error => {
  console.error('Error posting message:', error);
});
```

Make sure to replace `process.env.SLACK_TOKEN` with your actual Slack token. You can create a Slack app, enable the API, and get your token from there: https://api.slack.com/authentication/basics.

Also, replace `#general` with the channel you want to post the message to.

Note that this is a basic example and may not cover all the use cases or edge cases. For more advanced Slack integrations, you might want to consider using a dedicated Slack SDK or a more robust library like `slack-sdk`.

