```css
.circle {
  fill: radial-gradient(white, lightblue);
  filter: drop-shadow(15px 15px 15px gray);
  transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
  background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #fff, #ffcccc);
  box-shadow: 10px 10px 5px 0px rgba(0,0,0,0.75);
  border-radius: 70%;
  transform: rotateX(10deg) rotateY(5deg);
  box-shadow: 0 5px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.5), 0 -5px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
}
```

In this example, we added `transform` property to rotate the circle along the X and Y axes. We also added two box shadows with different offsets to create a 3D effect. You can adjust the rotation angles and shadow sizes to achieve the desired look.

