```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    // Sort the set by age in ascending order (default)
    if ($order == 'asc') {
        usort($set, function($a, $b) {
            return $a['age'] - $b['age'];
        });
    }

    // Sort the set by age in descending order
    elseif ($order == 'desc') {
        usort($set, function($a, $b) {
            return $b['age'] - $a['age'];
        });
    }
}
```

To use this function, simply call it with your set and desired order:

```php
$set = [
    ['name' => 'Alice', 'address' => '123 Main St', 'age' => 25],
