To improve the efficiency of your code, consider the following optimizations:

1. Use `useMemo` to memoize the `prompts.data` array, as it doesn't change frequently and re-fetching it on every render can be expensive.
2. Use `useEffect` to fetch the `prompts.data` array only when the component mounts or when the `setSelectedTargetPrompt`, `setEditedPrompt`, or `setEditedName` state changes. This will prevent unnecessary API calls.
3. Use `useState` to manage the `isOpen` state instead of using the `onOpen` and `onClose` functions from `useDisclosure`. This will allow you to control the modal visibility more efficiently.
4. Use `useCallback` to create a memoized version of the `onClick` function for the "New/Edit Prompt" button. This will prevent unnecessary re-rendering of the function when the component updates.
5. Use `useRef` to store the `selectedTargetPrompt`, `editedName`, and `editedPrompt` values instead of storing them in the component state. This will allow you to access them more efficiently and avoid unnecessary re-rendering of the component when these values change.
6. Use `useImperativeHandle` to expose a ref to the modal element, which will allow you to control its visibility and focus programmatically.
7. Use `useLayoutEffect` to update the modal position when the window size changes. This will ensure that the modal stays in a visible and accessible position.

